From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:59:17 +0000
Subject: PCI: rockchip-host: Enable async probe by default

The probe waits for the link to come up, and with an empty slot it holds
the deferred-probe worker for about 0.7 s. On ROCK Pi 4 the I/O-domain
driver then binds after the SD card has switched to 1.8 V, and UHS
tuning fails ("All phases bad!").

Probe asynchronously, as commit c0e1eb441b1d ("PCI: qcom: Enable async
probe by default") does for the Qualcomm host driver.

Signed-off-by: Igor Velkov <iav@iav.lv>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
index 2025a6b..0192b37 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-rockchip-host.c
@@ -1094,10 +1094,11 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, rockchip_pcie_of_match);
 static struct platform_driver rockchip_pcie_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "rockchip-pcie",
 		.of_match_table = rockchip_pcie_of_match,
 		.pm = &rockchip_pcie_pm_ops,
+		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 	.probe = rockchip_pcie_probe,
 	.remove = rockchip_pcie_remove,
 };
 module_platform_driver(rockchip_pcie_driver);
